## Reference

The course draws each texture on a 320 by 200 canvas with `c` the 2d context and `r` a seeded random in [0, 1). `pix(c, fn)` fills every pixel from `fn(x, y) -> [r, g, b]`, `noise(c, amount, r)` adds grain, `g2(x, y, cx, cy, sigma)` is a gaussian blob, `ramp(stops, t)` interpolates a colour ramp and `mix(a, b, t)` lerps two colours. Use the code for the look of each texture, in the palette's colours rather than the course's.

